{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_shift function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            # Convert to 0-indexed alphabet position, shift backward by 5,\n            # apply modulo 26 for wrap-around, then convert back to character ordinal.\n            shifted_ord = ((ord(ch) - ord('a') - 5) % 26) + ord('a')\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_ord))\n        else:\n            # Non-lowercase alphabetic characters remain unchanged.\n            decoded_chars.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
