{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "def largest_prime_factor(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assume n > 1 and is not a prime.\"\"\"\n    import math\n\n    max_prime = -1\n\n    # Handle the case of 2\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        max_prime = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors from 3 up to sqrt(n)\n    for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n        while n % i == 0:\n            max_prime = i\n            n //= i\n\n    # If n is still greater than 2, it must be the largest prime factor itself\n    if n > 2:\n        max_prime = n\n\n    return max_prime"}
