{"task_id": "HumanEval/148", "solution": "def bf(planet1, planet2):\n    '''\n    Returns a tuple of planets whose orbits are located between planet1 and planet2, sorted by proximity to the sun.\n    Returns an empty tuple if planet1 or planet2 are not correct planet names.\n    '''\n    PLANETS = [\n        \"Mercury\", \"Venus\", \"Earth\", \"Mars\", \"Jupiter\", \"Saturn\", \"Uranus\", \"Neptune\"\n    ]\n\n    def _get_planet_index(planet_name: str) -> int:\n        try:\n            return PLANETS.index(planet_name)\n        except ValueError:\n            return -1\n\n    idx1 = _get_planet_index(planet1)\n    idx2 = _get_planet_index(planet2)\n\n    if idx1 == -1 or idx2 == -1:\n        return ()\n\n    start_idx = min(idx1, idx2)\n    end_idx = max(idx1, idx2)\n\n    # If the planets are the same or adjacent, there are no planets between them.\n    if end_idx - start_idx <= 1:\n        return ()\n\n    return tuple(PLANETS[start_idx + 1:end_idx])"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "def x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"A simple program which should return the value of x if n is \n    a prime number and should return the value of y otherwise.\n\n    Examples:\n    for x_or_y(7, 34, 12) == 34\n    for x_or_y(15, 8, 5) == 5\n    \n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Helper function to check if a number is prime.\n    def is_prime(num):\n        if num <= 1:\n            return False\n        if num == 2 or num == 3:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    if is_prime(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y"}
